{# ------------------------------------------------------- C HOW WE THINK #}
<section class="think" id="how-we-think" aria-labelledby="think-h2">
  <div class="think-head">
    <p class="mod-label">How we think</p>
    <h2 class="think-h2" id="think-h2">What is genuinely changing, and what isn&rsquo;t.</h2>
    <p class="think-intro">The same few ideas shape every engagement, translated here rather than stated as internal methodology.</p>
  </div>
  {# One console: a continuous near-black field with a shared signal rail;
     three numbered zones, one ochre marker each, cream type on the field. #}
  <ol class="console">
    <li class="zone">
      <div class="zone-rail"><span class="zone-idx">01</span><span class="zone-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
      <h3>Start with the ecosystem, not the platform</h3>
      <p>We begin with the people around a product and the relationships between them, not with the assumption that the answer is another Discord, forum, or community platform.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="zone">
      <div class="zone-rail"><span class="zone-idx">02</span><span class="zone-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
      <h3>Research before prescription</h3>
      <p>Community, DevRel, partnerships, and advocacy increasingly overlap. We look at how participation actually works before recommending where teams, programs, or platforms should sit.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="zone">
      <div class="zone-rail"><span class="zone-idx">03</span><span class="zone-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
      <h3>Build for what is changing</h3>
      <p>AI is changing discovery, support, content creation, and product adoption. We combine hands-on operating experience with ongoing practitioner research to understand what is genuinely changing, and what isn&rsquo;t.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

